From 2dcd24031b0c88fd1aed602cb127b2960dd222b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:50:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] round C1.8: AGENTS goes through the Clerk card and lands on
 the AI Agent portal

Tao, 2026-09-11: every agent sign-in entry goes through the Clerk card and,
after sign-in, lands on the AI Agent portal.

- app/lib/clerk-entry.ts
  * AGENT_PORTAL_NEXT = /agent-loop/agent.
  * /agent-login joins RETIRED_LOGIN_PATHS (now two entries), with its own
    default landing: /agent-loop/login -> /agent-loop/customer (unchanged),
    /agent-login -> /agent-loop/agent.
  * retiredEntryRedirect(pathname, rawNext): a valid next on the old link
    is kept, so the agent page's own signed-out bounce
    (/agent-loop/login?next=/agent-loop/agent) now returns to the agent
    page instead of the customer page. Other query parameters (the old
    forms' resume/reason/order) are dropped.
- middleware.ts: passes the old link's next through; comments updated.
  Nothing else changes: the header's AGENTS link, bookmarks and the legacy
  agent pages that bounce to /agent-login all reach the card this way.

Unchanged: app/agent-login/page.tsx (byte-identical, still served while
Clerk is off), LoginMenu, every page. A half configured deployment now
refuses /agent-login (503) as it already does /client-login.

Tests (counts unchanged: entry-rules 20, middleware 16, run-all 104)
- test-entry-rules: "golden route is NOT retired" becomes "retired to the
  card, lands on the portal" (+ next kept / refused); "only the test-only
  alias" becomes "exactly two old entries". 2 fail on the old code.
- test-middleware: /agent-login -> 307 /client-login?next=%2Fagent-loop%2Fagent
  (incl. trailing slash and old resume/order query); /agent-loop/login keeps
  a valid next; misconfigured now refuses /agent-login. 3 fail on the old code.
No hunk touches a line the relay snapshot redacts.

